determinism screen
------------------
Every case was run TWICE with the identical command line and compared on every
.sol field except 'total time (s)' and 'time building kernel and buckets (s)'.
  204 cases run, 199 deterministic, 5 excluded by this screen (see EXCLUSIONS.tsv)

LIMITATION FOUND LATER: two agreeing runs are NOT enough for a marginal instance.
neos-1456979 passed the 2-run screen for several cases yet a 3-run repeat on the
same baseline binary produced up to 3 DISTINCT outcomes per case (config17: 3/3
distinct for every seed). All 8 of its remaining cases were therefore removed:
see stability-neos-1456979.tsv for the evidence. Final golden set: 191 cases.
If this set is ever rebuilt, screen with >= 3 runs, not 2.
The 5 exclusions are wall-clock-sensitive rather than clock-limited: none hit its
time limit, but the per-bucket budget time_left/(num_buckets+1) shifts slightly
between runs, so a bucket completes a different number of FP iterations.

